<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/GD8EEKQ5/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/GD8EEKQ5/>;
    dc:modified '2026-06-08T13:55:31'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'ocean_number_content_of_large_pelagic_fish'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Content" indicates a quantity per unit area. Large pelagic fish (>250 g) live in waters near the surface or throughout the water column (e.g., tuna, marlin, pelagic sharks).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::GD8EEKQ5'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/JD5K04M5/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/JD5K04M5/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/JD5K04M5/>;
    dc:modified '2026-06-08T13:55:31'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'ocean_number_content_of_mature_individuals_of_biological_taxon'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Content" indicates a quantity per unit area. Mature individuals refer to individuals that have reached sexual maturity. "Biological taxon" is a name or other label identifying an organism or a group of organisms as belonging to a unit of classification in a hierarchical taxonomy. There must be an auxiliary coordinate variable with standard name biological_taxon_name to identify the taxon in human readable format and optionally an auxiliary coordinate variable with standard name biological_taxon_identifier to provide a machine-readable identifier. See Section 6.1.2 of the CF convention (version 1.8 or later) for information about biological taxon auxiliary coordinate variables.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::JD5K04M5'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/KBKBXYAD/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/KBKBXYAD/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/KBKBXYAD/>;
    dc:modified '2026-06-08T13:55:31'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'mass_concentration_of_biological_taxon_of_immature_individuals_expressed_as_wet_weight_in_sea_water'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Biomass of immature individuals of various fish species as identified by their taxonomic name (e.g. Sardina pilchardus) in gram per m3. "Biological taxon" is a name or other label identifying an organism or a group of organisms as belonging to a unit of classification in a hierarchical taxonomy. There must be an auxiliary coordinate variable with standard name biological_taxon_name to identify the taxon in human readable format and optionally an auxiliary coordinate variable with standard name biological_taxon_identifier to provide a machine-readable identifier. See Section 6.1.2 of the CF convention (version 1.8 or later) for information about biological taxon auxiliary coordinate variables. Immature individuals refer to individuals that have not yet reached sexual maturity.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::KBKBXYAD'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/T4QVHCST/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/T4QVHCST/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/T4QVHCST/>;
    dc:modified '2026-06-08T13:55:31'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'change_in_sea_surface_height_due_to_pole_tide'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Sea surface height" is a time-varying quantity. The specification of a physical process by the phrase "due_to_" process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. Tides are a significant contributor to the observed sea surface height; the pole tide occurs due to variations in the earth\'s rotation.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::T4QVHCST'^^xsd:string .
